       "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000305",
       "source": "PubMed",
       "id": "19805282"
      }
     ],
     "value": "Structural subunit of the mitochondrial Glu-tRNA(Gln) amidotransferase complex GatCAB. GatCAB allows the formation of correctly charged Gln-tRNA(Gln) through the transamidation of misacylated Glu-tRNA(Gln) in the mitochondria (PubMed:19805282). The reaction takes place in the presence of glutamine and ATP through an activated gamma-phospho-Glu-tRNA(Gln) (By similarity). This subunit probably forms a belt that wraps around the interface of the catalytic subunits A and B to stabilize the complex (Probable)"
    }
   ],
   "commentType": "FUNCTION"
  },
